cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RehabKG in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "RehabKG: A Rehabilitation Knowledge Graph Integrating Functioning Ontologies, Clinical Datasets, and Therapeutic Exercises"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Center for Bioinformatics and Computational Biology"
    given-names: "University of Delaware"
    alias: "udel-cbcb"
repository-code: "https://github.com/udel-cbcb/RehabKG"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  RehabKG is a Neo4j knowledge graph that integrates rehabilitation and
  ontologies (ICF, HPO, Uberon, Mondo, EXMO, COPPER, KHMO, PAIN, CBHA,
  REHABO, and other retained sources) with therapeutic exercise catalogs,
  clinical-trial records,
  and rehabilitation outcome data. Every graph edge carries a
  provenance contract (method, match_type, confidence, source,
  review_status), and curated clinical edges flow through a
  clinician-in-the-loop review workflow. The graph supports Cypher
  querying, a Streamlit dashboard, a read-only FastAPI service, and
  evaluation tooling for rehabilitation knowledge-discovery research.
keywords:
  - knowledge graph
  - rehabilitation
  - ontology
  - ICF
  - clinical trials
  - provenance
  - human-in-the-loop
notes: >-
  Source datasets and ontologies have their own licenses; see
  docs/DATA_SOURCES.md. MOTU patient data in the demo graph is
  synthetic/de-identified and must not be used for clinical care.
